    "facts_line": "2026-10-27 (Tuesday, after the close), 5 days out -- from the earnings calendar, consensus EPS 6.25.",
    "why": "Q3 must show DRAM prices rising again after Q2's shortfall and revenue above the 99.68T consensus, or the tight-supply case stays a forecast."
  },
  "reasons": [
    "Because DRAM tight supply is expected to persist into 2028, pricing holds and Q2's 76% operating margin runs for years rather than one quarter.",
    "Because cloud capex rises 98% in 2026 and 50% in 2027 while memory's share goes from 47% to 68%, memory spend grows faster than the capex funding it.",
    "Because long-term supply agreements now lock volumes and prices, the earnings behind the 5.37x forward PE are contracted rather than spot, so the market is discounting a spot-cycle peak that no longer exists."
  ],
  "watch": [
    "Revenue vs the 99.68T consensus: confirm above; break if DRAM average selling prices fall short again as they did in Q2.",
    "Operating margin vs Q2's 76%: confirm at or above; break on compression from won strength or DRAM price give-back.",
    "HBM4 [fourth-generation high-bandwidth memory] timing: confirm a Q4 sales ramp is guided; break if it slips into 2027.",
    "Q4 guidance on memory pricing: confirm prices still rising into year-end; break if management flags oversupply or lockup selling."
  ],
